  "chapter": 48,
  "sortOrder": 19048,
  "verseCount": 14,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, in the mountain of his holiness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Beautiful for situation, the joy of the whole earth, is mount Zion, on the sides of the north, the city of the great King.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "God is known in her palaces for a refuge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For, lo, the kings were assembled, they passed by together.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "They saw it, and so they marvelled; they were troubled, and hasted away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Fear took hold upon them there, and pain, as of a woman in travail.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish with an east wind.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the LORD of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "We have thought of thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "According to thy name, O God, so is thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah be glad, because of thy judgments.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Mark ye well her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell it to the generation following.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:48:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For this God is our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide even unto death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 48:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:48:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
